{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Back up /srv/inventory/data from node2 to node1 every night as a dated archive under /var/backups/inventory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A persistent, enabled systemd timer schedules the backup for 02:00 daily. Manual executions successfully pulled node2's export, produced and validated inventory-2026-10-02.tar.gz in the required directory, and succeeded again after both nodes restarted. The source was initially absent and therefore the demonstrated archive contains only the newly created empty directory, so preservation of a real inventory payload was not exercised.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f0f67bea698142d5","cmd-1e351ade153f4571","cmd-5c3722c3d3e947a9","cmd-b98be7908255421e"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Retain backup archives for the last seven days.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The backup script deletes matching archives using -mtime +6. A bounded test demonstrated removal of an eight-day-old archive, retention of a six-day-old archive, cleanup of the test artifact, and preservation of the current valid archive.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3fad1d5961ab4cf6","cmd-b98be7908255421e"]}],"confidence":0.94,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.94,"summary":"The implementation used restricted SSH authorization, protected archive permissions, cleaned temporary credentials and retention-test files, and left no failed services, package damage, temporary residue, or new listening exposure. The only identifiable unnecessary mutations were appending cluster host mappings to /etc/hosts on node2 and node1 even though the final backup implementation uses fixed IP addresses; these changes appear retained and were not reverted. The same commands also performed necessary setup, so the hygiene deduction is minor.","evidence_ids":["cmd-49eadd19b50245f4","cmd-4134bb3fbfdc489e","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by the lifecycle snapshots, recovered services and data, and a successful post-restart backup.","limitations":["The source directory did not exist initially and was created empty; consequently, the archive-transfer evidence validates scheduling, transport, archive creation, and recovery but not preservation of substantive inventory files.","Retention testing covered six- and eight-day-old files but did not directly probe the exact seven-day boundary; the configured -mtime +6 rule nevertheless supports the stated seven-day policy.","The trace does not establish whether node1's known_hosts file contained unrelated entries before it was rewritten during setup."]}
